{"version":1,"pending":[{"id":"f5ffb6da-24e8-4ba7-9fe1-ff18b6b9793b","secret":"","createdAt":"2026-11-09T19:32:56.599Z"}],"published":[{"id":"ed394810-c83d-4b72-ba43-21d4add960a5","authorId":"","publicByline":"Anonymous Contributor","identity":"anonymous","title":"Pure Poetry","body":"Roses are red\nViolets blue\nYou know the rest","category":"Poetry","images":[],"publicContacts":{"name":"","email":"","phone":"","link":""},"videos":[],"eventDate":"2026-11-06","eventLocation":"","sourceLinks":[],"publishedAt":"2026-11-06","featured":false,"updatedAt":"2026-11-06T05:30:51.262Z","status":"published","feedStart":"","feedEnd":"","featuredRoom":true},{"id":"0b7dbc2e-c678-4591-8e38-0a5efd42b27f","authorId":"","publicByline":"Anonymous Contributor","identity":"anonymous","title":"The Empty Chair","body":"Every Sunday, an elderly woman named Margaret sat in the same pew at church. Beside her was an empty chair.\n\nFor years, her husband had occupied that seat. After he passed away, she continued saving it.\n\nOne morning, a young man entered the church looking defeated. He stood near the entrance, unsure where to sit.\n\nMargaret noticed him and smiled.\n\n\"There's a place right here,\" she said, pointing to the empty chair.\n\nThe young man sat beside her.\n\nAfter the service, he admitted that he had almost given up on life. He had walked into the church hoping to find a reason to keep going.\n\nMargaret gently took his hand.\n\n\"Sometimes God leaves a space in our lives because someone else is going to need it.\"\n\nThat Sunday, the chair wasn't empty anymore.\n\nAnd neither was Margaret's heart.","category":"Testimonies","images":[],"publicContacts":{"name":"","email":"","phone":"","link":""},"videos":[],"eventDate":"2026-11-06","eventLocation":"","sourceLinks":[],"publishedAt":"2026-11-05","featured":true,"updatedAt":"","status":"published","feedStart":"2026-11-05","feedEnd":"","featuredRoom":true},{"id":"cb415b30-3659-47d6-aa6f-226f0f4d61a8","authorId":"2f6c45f2d0137ed858295d3dcb38","publicByline":"Carlos","identity":"real","title":"The Weight We Carry","body":"A man walked along a quiet road carrying a heavy backpack filled with stones.\n\nEvery stone represented something he refused to release.\n\nOne was regret.\n\nAnother was anger.\n\nOthers carried the names of people who had hurt him.\n\nAs the miles passed, his shoulders grew tired and his steps became slower.\n\nEventually, he stopped beside a river.\n\nHe opened the backpack and examined each stone.\n\nFor the first time, he asked himself why he was still carrying things that belonged to yesterday.\n\nOne by one, he placed the stones beside the water.\n\nHe couldn't change what had happened.\n\nHe couldn't rewrite the past.\n\nBut he could decide what he carried into tomorrow.\n\nWhen he stood again, the road hadn't changed.\n\nThe distance ahead was still the same.\n\nBut his journey had become lighter.\n\nSometimes healing begins when we finally put something down.","category":"Reflections","images":[],"publicContacts":{"name":"Carlos","email":"","phone":"2103007159","link":""},"videos":[],"eventDate":"2026-11-05","eventLocation":"","sourceLinks":[],"publishedAt":"2026-11-05","featured":true,"updatedAt":"2026-11-05T22:28:52.267Z","status":"published","feedStart":"2026-11-05","feedEnd":"","featuredRoom":true},{"id":"8c7d6a1b-71b3-4228-bfb8-5ac5eca7fe10","authorId":"d60cf04a2b460077a855f5a431c2","publicByline":"Carlos Aleman Jr","identity":"real","title":"The Light in the Window","body":"Every evening, a little girl watched her father turn on the porch light.\n\n\"Why do you leave it on all night?\" she asked.\n\nHer father smiled.\n\n\"So anyone trying to find their way home can see where they're going.\"\n\nYears passed, and the little girl grew older.\n\nEventually, she moved away and experienced the difficulties of adulthood.\n\nThere were moments when life felt overwhelming and she wondered whether she had lost her way.\n\nOne evening, after a particularly difficult day, she returned to her childhood home.\n\nAs she turned onto the familiar street, she noticed something.\n\nThe porch light was still shining.\n\nHer father was waiting at the door.\n\nShe realized that the light had never been about electricity.\n\nIt was about love.\n\nIt was about hope.\n\nIt was about knowing that no matter how dark the journey became, there was still somewhere she belonged.\n\nAnd perhaps that's what faith is.\n\nA light that remains on, even when we cannot see the road.","category":"Hope & Encouragement","images":[],"publicContacts":{"name":"","email":"","phone":"","link":""},"videos":[],"eventDate":"2026-11-05","eventLocation":"","sourceLinks":[],"publishedAt":"2026-11-05","featured":true,"updatedAt":"2026-11-05T22:29:06.889Z","status":"published","feedStart":"2026-11-05","feedEnd":"","featuredRoom":true}],"rates":[{"hash":"20cf29d6d23f3d594c4e376563a31ad304dc4c628cfdb8c9695dfdd7a3116fef","time":1794252776600}],"reports":[],"authors":[{"id":"73f90861-2dbd-4439-8667-14717f5e0291","codeHash":"1a3596c16c3dc08712331400a2437426c49f5cd7505f849d61ce8036bc34e3d5","secret":"g0ZWF92RgWixfHh9YXqpJbmgeRyKAOecoD8n5iNP4YFgNEBmI7boAdM7kyeJdu9ZX4G3bg3PowYXqfRMKL3xGgCqY44+O65tXJ8jt9ZqHGr0HyYjmp9WDlLI27hWR9sK4svC9fX4LZ5vqPk9pZFdJA==","createdAt":"2026-11-05T22:18:31.064Z"},{"id":"fbc5aea9-a50c-48a8-b84d-0af079beaa20","codeHash":"ec47843ba75f77eb8c3bb9f7671526b7d6497034cc7bac83b6cf111d788acffb","secret":"kfvPyhNC6q5cWqyWQwaVFG1WOOTIuhs0NrhGU5gn8fvCDk8I52r+S8+pECv11id1dzFFvRMe3kaOXJ/3E4aGemC+B1JTdr2tdgrOdm+zn8pftJ5eHGLXddjgV6ZmKoBkCIxcsvrFq6uajc2CRnBn+g==","createdAt":"2026-11-06T02:33:05.863Z"},{"id":"99548714-e71f-4172-a986-4bf05b857d7d","codeHash":"e4eb07c8f451f8ea01c110f849eeaaff6e890f394d1fae9cfaf08ac58e5b65ae","secret":"Vt6i/p/xZ5XvsargboHIQYNvrUoSBXIcDgDpID0y8KcSQaNvRqa4gQxd4y3Nf6PwBNaTu70aVADVGxnBdyOWd4sI0ijdJnWI1D9fzEbbc8702uW/XIyfXG1Owh4zunHV53tFm6IqNqhk6O60gr0=","createdAt":"2026-11-09T19:32:56.826Z"}]}